{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Extend the 20% Business Rates Cut to Restaurants in England",
        "additional_details": "Restaurants make a significant contribution to employment, tourism, local supply chains and high streets. Despite facing comparable operating cost pressures, they are excluded from the additional 20% business rates reduction announced for eligible pubs, social clubs and live music venues. \r\n\r\nExtending equivalent relief to eligible restaurants would support investment, protect jobs and promote a more consistent approach to business rates across the hospitality sector.",
        "background": "We ask the UK Government to extend the announced 20% reduction in business rates bills for eligible pubs, social clubs and live music venues to eligible restaurants in England, including independent operators, national chains and franchise-operated sites.",
